\ Protocol annotation fidelity in AOT runtime-image mode. The bounded
\ word's stack effect serializes its protocol bound as a slot reference
\ into the protocol descriptor slot table; the loader restores the
\ annotation at startup, so introspection sees the bound instead of a
\ bare untyped parameter.
\
\ The fixture module is the only entry in the rehydrated module cache;
\ `native.>word` reads the word's stack effect straight from it. The
\ raw introspection record is indexed directly: element 1 is the
\ stack-effect record { inputs outputs }, a param is { name row? quot
\ annotation }, and `native.>protocol-info` renders the annotation as
\ { name methods protocol_id }.

use "fixtures/aot_protocol_annotation_dep.1z" ;

module-cache get @values #first
bounded-caller: native.>word
1 #nth 0 #nth 0 #nth 3 #nth
native.>protocol-info 0 #nth print-line
